<title>BRAZIL: MOTOR RACING-GRID POSITIONS FOR BRAZILIAN GRAND PRIX.</title>
<headline>MOTOR RACING-GRID POSITIONS FOR BRAZILIAN GRAND PRIX.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-03-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Grid positions for Sunday's</p>
<p>Brazilian Grand Prix motor race after Saturday's qualifying</p>
<p>session:</p>
<p>1. Jacques Villeneuve (Canada) Williams one minute and</p>
<p>16.004 seconds</p>
<p>  2. Michael Schumacher (Germany) Ferrari	1:16.594</p>
<p>  3. Gerhard Berger (Austria) Benetton	   1:16.644</p>
<p>  4. Mika Hakkinen (Finland) McLaren	     1:16.692</p>
<p>  5. Olivier Panis (France) Prost		  1:16.756</p>
<p>  6. Jean Alesi (France) Benetton		  1:16.757</p>
<p>  7. Giancarlo Fisichella (Italy) Jordan	 1:16.912</p>
<p>8. Heinz-Harald Frentzen (Germany) Williams  1:16.924</p>
<p>  9. Damon Hill (Britain) Arrows		   1:17.090</p>
<p> 10. Ralf Schumacher (Germany) Jordan	    1:17.175</p>
<p> 11. Rubens Barrichello (Brazil) Stewart	1:17.259</p>
<p> 12. David Coulthard (Britain) McLaren	  1:17.262</p>
<p> 13. Johnny Herbert (Britain) Sauber	    1:17.409</p>
<p> 14. Eddie Irvine (Britain) Ferrari	     1:17.527</p>
<p> 15. Shinji Nakano (Japan) Prost		  1:17.999</p>
<p> 16. Pedro Diniz (Brazil) Arrows		  1:18.095</p>
<p> 17. Jarni Trulli (Italy) Minardi		 1:18.336</p>
<p> 18. Ukyo Katayama (Japan) Minardi		1:18.557</p>
<p> 19. Nicola Larini (Italy) Sauber		 1:18.644</p>
<p> 20. Jan Magnussen (Denmark) Stewart	    1:18.773</p>
<p> 21. Jos Verstappen (Netherlands) Tyrrell     1:18.885</p>
<p> 22. Mika Salo (Finland) Tyrrell		  1:19.274</p>
<p>Note: Villeneuve's average speed was 203.294 kph.</p>
</text>
